The mailbox exists since #191: refs/karr-foundation/questions/<id>/ask and .../answer, `karr-foundation ask` / `answer`, and App::karr::Foundation::Questions->resolve returning answered / open / overdue plus the policy that applies when nobody answers. Nothing in the runner reads any of it yet.

A chain step of `kind: question` (#189) can be written and depended on, but no tick waits on one, none fires `use_default` when the deadline passes, and none calls the planner on `escalate_to_ai`. The link is in the data already -- `ask --step ID` records which step a question belongs to -- and nothing walks it.

What is missing: a ready step of kind question resolves its question and then (a) stays pending while the answer is `open`, so its dependents wait and everything else in the chain keeps running, (b) is done once the answer is there, with the answer in the run log, (c) on `overdue` does what the policy says -- block keeps waiting, use_default takes the default, escalate_to_ai calls the coordination agent. Also to decide: whether such a step asks the question itself when none exists yet, or whether the planner always writes the question first.

Deliberately not part of #191, which was the mailbox and its two commands.
